{number: 113}
{title: A Shelter in the Time of Storm}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
The [F] Lord's our Rock, in Him we hide,
A Shelter in the time of [C7] storm;
Secure whatever ill betide,
A [F] Shelter in the [C7] time of [F] storm.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Oh, [Bb] Jesus is a Rock in a [F] weary land,
A weary land, a [C7] weary land;
Oh, [Bb] Jesus is a Rock in a [F] weary land,
A [F] Shelter in the [C7] time of [F] storm.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
A [F] shade by day, defense by night,
A Shelter in the time of [C7] storm;
No fears alarm, no foes affright,
A [F] Shelter in the [C7] time of [F] storm.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
The [F] raging storms may round us beat,
A Shelter in the time of [C7] storm;
We'll never leave our safe retreat,
A [F] Shelter in the [C7] time of [F] storm.
{end_of_verse}
